@title STORY • SUKI: HELD TOGETHER WITH TAPE
@bg dorm_room_morning
You're Suki Bennett. You wake up to three texts from Jayden: "morning." "you good?" "we should talk." You've been dating him for a year. It's felt like a group project for six months.
And one from Jamal: "you left your water bottle in the long jump pit. i'll bring it." Nothing else. He never says anything else. That's the problem. You read it eleven times.
> [Good] Text Jayden back first. He's your boyfriend. -> a1
> [Bad] Text Jamal back first. -> a2
> [Sweet] Text neither. Call your mom. -> a3
*a1
@add Suki_Truth 1
Suki: "morning ❤️ ya we should"
You add the heart out of habit. You notice you're adding it out of habit. That's the part that scares you.
@jump a_done
*a2
@add Suki_Jamal 2
Suki: "my hero lol"
Jamal: "lol"
You know exactly what you're doing. You do it anyway.
@jump a_done
*a3
@add Self 3
Your mom picks up on the first ring. Houston accent, TV in the background.
Mom: Baby! You sound sad. You sound sad, Suki. Who do I need to fight?
You laugh for the first time in a week. You don't tell her. But you feel lighter.
*a_done
@bg track_stadium_day
@show jayden
Jayden: Suki. Real talk. I don't think either of us is happy.
You've been waiting six months for him to say it. Now it's here and you want to scream.
Suki: Is this about Paris?
Jayden: (long pause) ...It's about us.
Suki: That's a yes.
> [Bitchy] "You've been in love with her since you were six. Everybody knows it, Jayden." -> b1
> [Sweet] "...I know. I'm not happy either." -> b2
> [Bold] Tell him about Jamal. All of it. Right now. -> b3
*b1
@add Self 1
Jayden: (quiet) That's fair.
Suki: Of course it's fair. I'm not mad you love her. I'm mad you made me feel crazy for noticing.
@jump end
*b2
@add Self 2
@add Jayden_Peace 2
Jayden takes your hand. Not like a boyfriend. Like a friend. It's the most honest he's been all year.
Jayden: We were good friends first.
Suki: We were great friends first.
@jump end
*b3
@add Suki_Truth 3
@add Self 2
You tell him. Kappa party. Jamal. The guilt. He doesn't yell. He just nods, like the last piece of a puzzle clicked.
Jayden: I'm glad it was Jamal. He's the best person I know.
Suki: (crying) That's so annoying of you.
*end
Suki Bennett is loud because quiet is where all her feelings live. This year, she's learning to turn the volume down long enough to hear them.
